{
  "explanation": "An attacker or compromised service running as the www-data user (UID 1005) attempted to execute administrative commands via sudo to escalate privileges to root. The PAM authentication failure log indicates that the attempt was unsuccessful because the correct password or credentials were not provided. This suggests a post-compromise activity where an adversary is attempting to gain full control over the host system.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Privilege Escalation",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Investigate the www-data user process and web application vulnerabilities that may have allowed initial execution or web shell deployment.",
    "Review and audit sudoers configuration to ensure least-privilege principles are strictly enforced and unnecessary sudo rights for web users are removed.",
    "Implement comprehensive endpoint monitoring and alerting for repeated sudo authentication failures."
  ]
}
